# Names only. Never commit real values. Copy to .env locally.

# --- Web (public, safe for browser) ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
# The ONLY Supabase values the browser/web app may know: project URL + the publishable key (formerly
# "anon"). Local stack: `supabase status` prints them; do not commit real values.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=   # legacy name, still accepted (the publishable name wins when both are set)
# The public site (job BS): its address (sitemap, share pictures) and the launch switch. Until NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_LIVE=1 the pages say noindex and robots.txt turns every crawler away.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_LIVE=0
# Public sign-up (job DH): "0" shows the early-access note instead of the form on /signup; unset leaves it open (what a local stack wants).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SIGNUP_OPEN=1
# Open sign-up (job AD / D2): at most this many sign-ups per hour from one address (a whole number from 1 to 1000; default 5).
# Counted in one web process's memory: a best-effort brake, not shared between instances. Server-side only, not a public value.
# SIGNUP_MAX_PER_HOUR=5
# The Plan and usage screens (job DK): unset or 0 = off. 1 = on (reads the plans and billing API of job DI; its fake payment provider only). mock = on with a fake provider kept in a cookie, for review only.
# PLAN_SCREENS=mock
# Website-only mode (job DQ): SITE_MODE=website serves only the public website and shows "Opening soon — book a demo" for /app, sign-in and sign-up. Unset = the usual behaviour. Search engines are let in only on stack19.com / www.stack19.com.
# SITE_MODE=website
# The "Book a demo / join the waitlist" form: unset = on in website mode, off otherwise; off | mock (keeps nothing) | 1 (the API's POST /v1/public/waitlist).
# WAITLIST=1
# Job DQ part 2 (DPDP): the marketing switch, Raise a grievance and sign-up's unticked marketing box: unset or 0 = off, mock = fake data, 1 = C1's API (contract-dpdp.md).
# DPDP_SCREENS=mock
# VOICE_SAMPLE_SCREENS=mock
# The live call screen, the outcomes and Settings > AI assistant (job DM): unset or 0 = off. mock = on with fake data kept in a cookie, for review only. 1 = on, for C1's APIs (not published yet: the parts say "Not available yet").
# CALL_SCREENS=mock
# OUTCOME_SCREENS=mock
# ASSISTANT_SCREENS=mock
# Job DP (night of 26 Oct): the call settings (Advanced), the own voice and the school's marks to parents: unset or 0 = off, mock = fake data, 1 = C1's API.
# CALL_SETTINGS_SCREENS=mock
# OWN_VOICE_SCREENS=mock
# MARKS_SCREENS=mock

# --- API (server-side only) ---
API_ENV=development
API_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
# Added in T002 (server-side only). T002 deliberately has NO service-role key: the API acts only
# with the user's own JWT so RLS always applies. Ask before adding one in a later ticket.
# Local stack: run `supabase start`; defaults below are filled in automatically when
# API_ENV=development (the publishable key is the only one you must set; it is a public key).
# Outside development the API REFUSES TO START unless every one of these is set (https only).
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=<publishable key>
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<legacy name of the same public key; still accepted, the publishable name wins>
# There is NO variable for a secret / service-role key and none is added (ADR 0017 c).
# SUPABASE_JWT_ISSUER=https://<project>.supabase.co/auth/v1
# SUPABASE_JWT_AUDIENCE=authenticated
# Suppression keys (T010, ADR 0020). The HMAC secret that turns an e-mail or a phone number into a key
# that survives erasure. One per environment, at least 16 characters (use 64 hex characters), NEVER committed, never logged.
# Outside development the API REFUSES TO START without it; in development it is optional (contacts then stay
# unkeyed and an erasure needs the Owner's explicit "allow without a key"). Generate: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
# Rotation: SUPPRESSION_HMAC_KEY_VERSION=<n>, SUPPRESSION_HMAC_KEY_PREVIOUS=<old secret> (matching only), SUPPRESSION_HMAC_KEY_PREVIOUS_VERSION=<n-1>
SUPPRESSION_HMAC_KEY=
# SUPABASE_JWKS_URL=https://<project>.supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json
# SUPABASE_JWT_ALGORITHMS=ES256
# Legacy HS256 projects only (also add HS256 to SUPABASE_JWT_ALGORITHMS):
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=
# Added in T006:
# LLM_PROVIDER=

# Agents (T006). OFF by default. The platform and per-workspace switches are in the database (operator-managed).
# AGENTS_ENABLED=false
# LLM_PROVIDER=fake   # a scripted model for development ONLY; refused when API_ENV is not "development"
# AGENTS_MAX_WORKERS=2
# AGENTS_MAX_QUEUE=8
# The real model adapter (provider "anthropic") stays OFF until ALL of these are set. The key is a secret: environment only.
# LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# LLM_MODEL=<model id of your choice; there is no default>
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<a dedicated key with a hard monthly spend cap set at the provider>
# LLM_INPUT_MICROS_PER_MTOK=<price per million input tokens, in millionths of the billing currency>
# LLM_OUTPUT_MICROS_PER_MTOK=<price per million output tokens, same unit>
# LLM_SPEND_CAP_CONFIRMED=false   # set to true only after the provider-side hard cap exists
# Optional, job AK K2b ("AI included, fair use"): the LIGHT model. A workspace over 100 % of its daily or monthly AI allowance is served by it until the reset (same provider
# and key). Set all three or none; its price also needs a row in agent_model_prices (docs/runbooks/agents-kill-switch.md). Unset = the main model keeps serving.
# LLM_LIGHT_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# LLM_LIGHT_INPUT_MICROS_PER_MTOK=90000000
# LLM_LIGHT_OUTPUT_MICROS_PER_MTOK=450000000
# Other providers behind the same port (job AK / K3): LLM_PROVIDER=openai | gemini | sarvam, each enabled ONLY by its own key (environment only; a typed-in hidden read is best, see docs/runbooks/model-bakeoff.md):
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# SARVAM_API_KEY=
# A model on THIS machine for free testing (Ollama): no key, address must be localhost, prices may be 0 (docs/runbooks/model-bakeoff.md):
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai_compat
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# LLM_MODEL=llama3.2:3b
# A hosted FREE-tier model for development only (job AN, ADR 0065; synthetic data only; refused unless API_ENV=development). The address must be exactly one of
# https://api.groq.com/openai/v1, https://api.cerebras.ai/v1, https://openrouter.ai/api/v1 (OpenRouter: a model id ending in :free). The key is a secret: environment only;
# `make dev-api-groq` reads it hidden and starts the API for you (docs/runbooks/main-agent-hosted-free.md).
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai_compat
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# LLM_API_KEY=

# --- Job CK: packs and social sign-up (server-side; names only) ---
# Where packages/packs lives (unset: the checkout's, then /srv/packages/packs in the container image).
# PACKS_DIR=
# Google / Facebook sign-up is OFFERED on the sign-up page only when the PUBLIC id is set here; unset = off. The id AND the secret are set in Supabase Auth
# (hosted: the dashboard, by hand; local: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / _SECRET and SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_FACEBOOK_APP_ID / _SECRET plus `enabled = true` in config.toml). docs/runbooks/social-sign-up.md
# AUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# AUTH_FACEBOOK_APP_ID=

# --- Job DR / A2: lead sources (all optional; unset = that door answers "not available") ---
# LEAD_INBOUND_DOMAIN=leads.example.com        # the forwarding addresses are leads+TOKEN@this-domain (needs an inbound mail provider)
# LEAD_INBOUND_SECRET=                         # header X-Inbound-Secret of the one global inbound address (POST /v1/lead-intake/mail)
# LEAD_DND_PROVIDER=off                        # off | fake (development only; no real lookup is chosen yet)
# META_LEAD_PROVIDER=off                       # off | fake (development only) | graph (needs META_APP_SECRET and META_PAGE_TOKEN, after Meta's app verification)
# META_APP_SECRET=
# META_PAGE_TOKEN=
# GOOGLE_SHEETS_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=         # shown to owners as the address to share a private sheet with (not used yet)
